Expected elements: present

Presence check first, with care on the scrubber. The identity bar shrinks rather than dropping anything at 1440: `← aztec`, hash, `Partial`, `block 101`, both stepping directions, a 160px scrubber track with a proportional cyan fill at ~10%, the readout `128 / 1315` beside it as a separate element, and the three named phases. Both required position elements are present and readable. `CODE` positioned at line 32, `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` tabbed with Call Trace open and seven frames, `VALUES` with ten values, `TRANSACTION` carrying the `DATA` provenance row. Nothing forbidden.

Where information genuinely lands, this is dense and scannable: the ACIR column is tabular across four magnitudes, the Values pane packs ten rows into 270px, the call trace shows depth with indent plus guides.

The density failures are all budget failures. 233px — 47% of the tab region — is empty below the last frame. The provenance paragraph takes 325px, 39% of the Transaction pane, to say what its badge already says, pushing seven metadata rows into the bottom 40%. The Code pane spends 136px on four header rows and then runs a 23px pitch on 13px type, showing 26 lines where 34 would fit at desktop-app line-height — in a pane whose own note says the position window is clipped.

Fixes: give the tab region's surplus to Values; tighten the listing pitch and cap the provenance prose.

Rating: 6/10

